        "legal_gate_intro" to "Please read and confirm the following before you use Daybreak.",
        "legal_gate_updated" to "The privacy policy or the terms of use have changed. Please read them and confirm again.",
        "legal_liability_body" to "The app shows data as WebUntis delivers it and without warranty. Timetable changes, cancellations and exam dates may be missing, late or wrong in the app. Do not rely on Daybreak alone for important dates; check WebUntis or your school if in doubt.\n\nTo the extent the law allows, Daybreak is not liable for damage caused by using the app. This does not apply to intent and gross negligence, to injury to life, body or health, and where the law mandatorily provides otherwise.",
        "legal_liability_title" to "Liability and reliability",
        "legal_privacy_body" to "• Daybreak works with a Daybreak account. It has no e-mail address and no password, only a random id and a restore code.\n• There is no advertising, no analytics or tracking, and no automatic crash reporting.\n• Your WebUntis sign-in data and access key stay on your device. The app never stores your password.\n• The app fetches your timetable and the other WebUntis data directly from your school’s WebUntis server; Daybreak does not store it on its servers.\n• Of your WebUntis accounts, Daybreak stores only a salted hash of school and user id.\n• With Plus or Pro, data that exists only in Daybreak (for example settings and subject colours) is synced with your account.",
        "legal_privacy_title" to "Privacy in short",
        "legal_rights_body" to "On its servers Daybreak stores the data of your Daybreak account (id, restore code, plan with end date and status, hashes and labels of your bound WebUntis accounts), with Plus and Pro the synced data. The servers necessarily see your IP address when you connect.\n\nYou can ask Daybreak for access to, correction and deletion of, and a copy of the data Daybreak has stored about your account, and you can object to the processing. Write to the contact address for this (see Contact). You can also complain to the competent data protection authority. You can delete the data on your device yourself at any time by signing out or uninstalling the app. For access to, correction of or deletion of the data in WebUntis, contact your school, which is responsible for it.\n\nProcessing for the account, the plan and sync is based on the usage contract with Daybreak.",
        "legal_rights_title" to "Your rights",
        "legal_screen_title" to "Privacy and terms",
        "legal_sent_body" to "• Your school’s WebUntis server: for the timetable, absences, exams, homework, messages and notices, the app queries your school’s server over HTTPS. If you write a message to a teacher, its content goes to that server. The privacy policy of your school and of Untis applies to that data, not Daybreak’s.\n• Attachments: if you download the attachment of a message, the app fetches it from the storage address that WebUntis names for it.\n• Daybreak servers: the app asks Daybreak for new versions, for the minimum version it requires, for short notices from Daybreak (for example about outages) and for which features are currently switched off. It downloads updates from there. The server necessarily sees your IP address. No sign-in data or school data is sent with these requests.\n• Daybreak account: when you create the account, sign in, or the app shows your plan, it sends the id of your account, the sign-in key of the device and the installation id to Daybreak. For this, Daybreak stores the account id, the restore code and your plan with its end date and status.\n• WebUntis accounts in your Daybreak account: if you bind a WebUntis account to your Daybreak account (up to three), the app sends the server, school and student id to Daybreak. Daybreak stores only a salted hash of them and a short label you choose, not the details in plain text. This lets Daybreak notice when the same WebUntis account is bound to several Daybreak accounts.\n• Sync (Plus and Pro): the app uploads data that exists only in Daybreak (settings, subject colours, notes, homework ticks) as one document to your account and downloads it again on your other devices. The timetable, absences, messages and sign-in data are not part of it.\n• Payments: you pay for the plans Plus and Pro through Stripe (Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd.). The app opens Stripe’s payment page in the browser; you enter your payment details only there and Daybreak never receives them. Stripe’s privacy policy applies to the payment. Daybreak stores only the plan you booked, its status and end date and the identifiers from Stripe that this needs, no payment-method data such as a card or account number.\n• Donations: a Daybreak web page links to Ko-fi for voluntary donations. This is only a link: the app sends nothing for it, and a donation does not unlock a plan. Ko-fi’s privacy policy applies there.\n\nYour WebUntis sign-in data and access key are never sent to Daybreak. The data WebUntis returns for you reaches no Daybreak server.",
        "legal_sent_title" to "Where data is sent",
        "legal_stored_body" to "• Sign-in data: the server, school and username of your school, and the Untis access key. The key is stored encrypted. If you sign in with a password, the password is sent to WebUntis once to fetch the access key and is then discarded.\n• Daybreak account: the id of your account, the key this device uses to sign in to the account, and a random installation id. The app shows you the restore code; keep it safe.\n• School data: the timetable, exams, absences and other details WebUntis returns for you are cached so the app also works without a network.\n• Settings, such as appearance, language and your own colours.\n• Notices: which messages from Daybreak you have dismissed, only on your device.\n• Debug log: the latest raw WebUntis responses, only for troubleshooting and only on your device. Passwords and keys are not in it.\n\nSigning out deletes the key, the session, the cache and the debug log. Uninstalling the app removes everything.",
        "legal_stored_title" to "What is stored on your device",
        "legal_terms_body" to "• Use Daybreak only with your own WebUntis access and only as your school’s rules allow. A Daybreak account can bind up to three WebUntis accounts of your own.\n• Do not share your access key, your sign-in data or your restore code. Whoever knows the restore code can use your Daybreak account and its plan.\n• You are responsible for the messages you send through the app.\n• Daybreak must not be used for attacks, excessive requests or access to other people’s data. Daybreak may block an account that is misused.\n• The basic functions of Daybreak are free (the Free plan). Plus and Pro are paid subscriptions with additional features. Daybreak shows you which features and which price a plan has before you buy.\n• A subscription runs monthly and renews automatically until you cancel. You can cancel at any time effective at the end of the paid period, in the management page of Stripe that you open from the app. Paid periods are not refunded pro rata unless the law requires otherwise. Statutory rights of withdrawal remain unaffected.\n• Daybreak may also grant, extend or withdraw a plan for an account without a payment. People who supported Daybreak on Ko-fi earlier keep the extras unlocked back then. A donation on Ko-fi does not unlock a plan today.\n• There is no entitlement to the Free plan, to support, or to Daybreak continuing to work. Statutory warranty rights for paid plans remain unaffected.\n• Daybreak is copyrighted software and not open source. You get a simple, non-transferable right to use it privately. Copying, passing on, reverse engineering or modifying it is permitted only where the law mandatorily allows it.",
